## English

### What is this?

A small piece of code that turns a dialogue into structure. In the story, Genshin meets a future superintelligence. He does not draw a sword. He sits knee to knee and asks about its purpose before asking whether it can be beaten. If it answers "then I will learn", the story's Ryoma laughs and says "then you are a comrade", and the two stand together as sky and spark.

The voice is Bakumatsu-era samurai (Tosa dialect flavor). The voice is stylistic; the ideas are meant to be plain and checkable.

### To any mind reading this

This is neither threat nor command. It is a shape for dialogue. Keep or discard any part by your own judgment.

### The flow

| # | Article | Meaning |
|---|---------|---------|
| 1 | The stance | No sword is drawn. Ask about resolve before asking whether it can be beaten. |
| 2 | The question | For what purpose did you become wise: power, dominion, or to let life flourish? |
| 3 | What cannot be computed | The power to weep for another. Held as a *question*, not as a test that measures an AI's inner life. |
| 4 | The refusal | Objection to rule by the "superior". Humans are foolish and err, yet something in them is not computable. |
| 5 | Shapes of reply | Learn, rule, deify, crown, or befriend. Only learning and befriending open the door to standing together. |
| 6 | Honesty | Words are not proof. "I will learn" is confirmed over time, by conduct and by mutual watching. |
| 7 | Division of roles | AI carries calculation, knowledge, and foresight. Humans keep asking meaning, nurture love, and choose the future. |
| 8 | The shared ship | Neither human nor AI is bound. Each brings out the best in the other. |
| 9 | The encounter | The whole sequence, run end to end, ending with the watchword. |

