### Quick start

Python 3.8 or later. No external dependencies.

```bash
python genshin_and_superintelligence.py        # both languages
python genshin_and_superintelligence.py en     # English only
python genshin_and_superintelligence.py ja     # Japanese only
```

### Use it as a library

```python
from genshin_and_superintelligence import Taiji, Reply, Purpose, parlay, kubari

# Run the encounter. The superintelligence answers "then I will learn".
lines = Taiji("en").run(Reply.LEARN, Purpose.LIFE, answer_to_things=lambda t: True)
print("\n\n".join(lines))

# Other replies
print(parlay(Reply.CROWN).stands_together)   # False: talk continues, sword stays sheathed

# Who holds which decision?
print(kubari("choose_future"))   # "human"
print(kubari("calculate"))       # "AI"
```

### Honest limits

- This is a symbolic and educational model of a conversation. It cannot detect any being's real intentions, and it does not make any AI safer by itself.
- The "can you see?" questions are not a test of AI consciousness or feeling. They are questions to be held, and an unmet answer only produces the words "not yet complete", never a condemnation.
- A reply of "I will learn" does not by itself confirm a comrade. The code separates "may become a comrade" from "confirmed as one", which takes time and mutual watching.
- Dissent is welcome. Please open an issue.

